#!/bin/sh
# Runs as root after the installer has put Netlane.app into /Applications:
# installs the VPN helper for the user at the screen (the installer already asked for the
# administrator password, so the app will not ask again) and opens Netlane for that user.
APP="/Applications/Netlane.app"
USER_ID=$(/usr/bin/stat -f %u /dev/console 2>/dev/null)
/usr/bin/xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine "$APP" 2>/dev/null || true
case "$USER_ID" in ''|0|*[!0-9]*) exit 0 ;; esac
# The app belongs to the user, so it can update itself later without an administrator password.
/usr/sbin/chown -R "$USER_ID":staff "$APP" || true
/bin/sh "$APP/Contents/Resources/install-helper.sh" "$APP/Contents/Resources" "$USER_ID" || true
/bin/launchctl asuser "$USER_ID" /usr/bin/open "$APP" || true
exit 0
